Subject: Resolved - POS terminal at Downtown restaurant could not connect
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 11:15:00 -0700
Message-ID: <incident-114@example.com>
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"

Incident INC-114 resolved.

Symptom: the restaurant POS terminal at the Downtown property could not connect and was
pulling a 169.254 address.

Root cause: the switch access port (Gi1/0/11 on SW-CORE-A) had been changed to VLAN 10
instead of the POS VLAN 55, so DHCP failed.

Resolution: set the port back to "switchport access vlan 55" and re-enabled PortFast +
BPDU Guard. Terminal pulled a 10.20.55.x address and connected. Verified stable.

Lesson learned: double-check access VLAN after any patching work.

Sam
